# CLAUDE.md — app/Http (framework HTTP layer)

Scope: `app/Http/`. Only framework HTTP plumbing lives here: `Middleware/` (its own `CLAUDE.md`), the base
`Controller.php`, shared controller `Concerns/` and the domain controllers (`Controllers/CLAUDE.md`). Domain
services, policies and jobs belong in their own `app/` directory; when in doubt, it does not go here.

## Hard rules

- **Every request is validated in its own FormRequest** (`app/Requests/CLAUDE.md`).
- **Every entity in a JSON response is its own API Resource**, collections and pagination included
  (`{data, meta}`): no `->toArray()`, raw model or hand-built array of one (`app/Resources/CLAUDE.md`).
  `response()->json()` only for a result that is no entity: an aggregate, a challenge, a redirect URL.
<!-- if:htmx -->
- **HTML responses are Blade views or fragments.** Full page vs fragment is decided in ONE place,
  `Controller::render()` (below); no action checks `HX-Request` itself. Templates render explicit fields, never a
  whole serialized model.
<!-- endif -->
- **Every route and action serves exactly one surface** (`routes/CLAUDE.md`); the surfaces have different trust
  levels.

<!-- if:htmx -->
## HTML caching (root `CLAUDE.md`, Non-negotiables)

**`CachePublicResponse`** (first in the `public` group, so a hit never reaches the limiter) serves anonymous
`GET`/`HEAD` from the default cache store (Redis; array in tests).
- **Key:** `page:{locale}:{build}:{sha256(normalised URL)}`. `build` is the Vite manifest hash, so a deploy retires
  every page that names old asset files.
- **Normalised URL** (`Services/Cache/PageCache::normalise`): host + path without trailing slash, sorted query minus
  `utm_*`/`fbclid`/`gclid`/`ref`. Query keys are kept per route from `{{app}}.route_query_keys`; anything else maps
  onto the canonical entry. htmx callers add `:hx`, plus `:{target}` when `HX-Target` names an allow-listed fragment
  id (`{{app}}.fragment_targets`), so a boosted full page and a targeted fragment never share an entry.
- **Stored:** `200 text/html` and tagged `301`s (status + `Location` in `PageEntry`). **Never stored:** a response
  with cookies or `no-store`, any request with `$request->user()`, a `HEAD` (decorated only).
- `ETag` = sha256 of the final body; `If-None-Match` → `304`.
- A prefetch or prerender miss (`Sec-Purpose`, `HX-Preloaded`) is stored like any request, warming the entry.
  Hover eagerness and `throttle:public` bound the volume.
- **Bypassed while Vite is hot** (`public/hot` exists): the manifest hash is null then, so edited views would keep
  serving old HTML. It answers `X-Cache: BYPASS` and `Cache-Control: no-store`.

**Invalidation is by versioned tag, never `Cache::tags()->flush()`** (a URL-only lookup cannot read tagged items,
and a wildcard flush walks every key).
- An entry records `{tag => version}` from `Services/Cache/CacheVersions` when stored and is stale once any moved. A
  write calls `CacheVersions::bump([...])`: one `INCR` per tag.
- `Services/Cache/InvalidatesPages::register()` (AppServiceProvider) bumps the entity's own tag and its reference
  tags on every `saved`/`deleted` of an admin-editable model.
- **Bulk upserts bypass model events**: they invalidate through a listener on the event that closes the bulk write,
  and warm in chunked jobs.
- Stale entries die by `{{app}}.page_cache.hard_ttl` (Redis is `noeviction`).

**Headers** on hit and miss, from `config/{{app}}.php`:
- `Cache-Control: public, max-age=60, s-maxage=300, stale-while-revalidate=3600` (`{{app}}.page_cache.cache_control`);
- `ETag`, `Vary: HX-Request, HX-Target, Accept-Encoding`, `X-Cache: HIT|MISS`;
- `PageMeta::$ttl` caps them per page (`max-age=ttl`, `s-maxage`/`swr` = `2·ttl`). Tags and ttl reach the middleware
  through `$request->attributes['page_meta']`, set by `Controller::render()` from `$data['meta']`.

**The CSP nonce is stored with the entry** and restored on a hit (`Vite::useCspNonce($stored)`; `SecurityHeaders`
reads it after `$next`).

**The fragment cache**: `Services/Cache/FragmentCache::remember(name, tags, fn)` wraps every slow aggregate in
`Cache::flexible` on a key holding the tags' current versions (`frag:{name}:v{versions}`).
<!-- if:tenancy -->
- An entry of tenant data has the tenant in its key: `frag:t:{tenant_id}:{name}:v{versions}`. The page cache never
  holds tenant data, because it stores no authenticated response.
<!-- endif -->
- **Cached values are plain data**: with `serializable_classes => false` (`config/cache.php`) Redis returns objects as
  `__PHP_Incomplete_Class`, while the test store passes them through. `FragmentCache` throws on objects; DTOs carry
  `toArray()`/`fromArray()`.
- Fragment routes pass a `PageMeta` too (tags only), or their entry lives on TTL alone.

**Authenticated responses are `Cache-Control: private, no-store`**, no exceptions: a personalised page in a shared
cache is a data leak. `bootstrap/app.php` applies it to the `web` group, and `routes/api.php` to the authenticated
api routes' group (Registered; `routes/CLAUDE.md`).
<!-- endif -->
<!-- unless:htmx -->
## Caching

**Authenticated responses are `Cache-Control: private, no-store`**, no exceptions: a personalised response in a shared
cache is a data leak. `bootstrap/app.php` applies it to the `web` group, and `routes/api.php` to the authenticated
api routes' group (Registered; `routes/CLAUDE.md`).
<!-- endif -->

## Registered (`bootstrap/app.php`)

There is no `Http/Kernel.php`, and **a missing registration fails silently**. Every alias goes in the one
`$middleware->alias([...])` call: each call replaces the whole alias map. The house names; create each under this name
when first needed:

- `cache.headers:private;no_store` appended to the `web` group. A successful `GET`/`HEAD` with a body answers
  `Cache-Control: no-store, private`. On `api` it goes on the authenticated routes' own group in `routes/api.php`
  (`auth:sanctum` beside it), never on the whole `api` group: a group's header is written last and would make a
  public API `GET` (`cache.headers:public;max_age=…` on its route) uncacheable.
- `RequestId` prepended globally; `SecurityHeaders` appended globally. The Horizon path is exempt: its dashboard is an
  inline-script SPA behind the gate.
<!-- if:htmx -->
- The CSP nonce is `Vite::useCspNonce()` per request, read in Blade with `Vite::cspNonce()`; only the JSON-LD tag and
  Vite's own tags use it. `script-src` allows `'inline-speculation-rules'` for the layout's Speculation Rules. While
  `public/hot` exists (never in production), the CSP also allows the origin in that file
  in `script-src`, `style-src` and `connect-src`, plus its `ws:` twin for HMR.
- Group `public` = `CachePublicResponse`, `throttle:public`, `SubstituteBindings`. Alias `htmx` = `HtmxOnly`,
  prepended to `SubstituteBindings` in the priority list.
- `Controller::render($view, $data, $fragment)` is the one htmx helper. It returns the named fragment only when the
  `HX-Target` header equals `$fragment`; a boosted navigation (no matching target) gets the full page. Head metadata
  travels as `App\Services\Seo\PageMeta` (`$data['meta']`), rendered by `x-layouts.app`; it also carries the cache
  tags and ttl.
<!-- endif -->
- `routes/api.php` under `/api/v1` (`withRouting(apiPrefix: 'api/v1')`).
<!-- if:htmx -->
  It is loaded with `api:` beside `then:`.
<!-- unless:auth-pages -->
- `AcceptJson` on Fortify's routes (`config/fortify.php` `middleware`) while its views are off (`resources/CLAUDE.md`,
  Auth pages), prepended to `AuthenticatesRequests` in the priority list (`routes/CLAUDE.md`).
<!-- endif -->
<!-- endif -->
<!-- unless:htmx -->
- `AcceptJson` on Fortify's routes (`config/fortify.php` `middleware`) and on the social link/unlink routes once
  built, prepended to `AuthenticatesRequests` in the priority list (`routes/CLAUDE.md`).
<!-- endif -->
<!-- if:spa -->
- `statefulApi()`, so Sanctum authenticates the SvelteKit app's `api` calls by the session cookie + XSRF token.
<!-- endif -->
<!-- if:tenancy -->
- Alias `tenant` = `ResolveTenant`, after `AuthenticatesRequests` in the priority list
  (`app/Http/Middleware/CLAUDE.md`, Tenancy).
<!-- endif -->
- Named rate limiters are defined in a service provider, never here (`app/Providers/CLAUDE.md`).
<!-- house:end -->
